messages:
maya: One more UX report: onboarding sample shows `for gen.Next()` and people are hitting weird behavior when auth refresh + ctx timeout coincide. We should simplify the recommended pattern.

ben: Can you describe the failure mode? Panic, leak, or ambiguous error?

maya: Mostly ambiguous errors or EOF; sometimes Close() reports a nil-pointer panic in older SDKs. Newer builds fixed panic but UX is still confusing.

owen: TL;DR: consumers expect a simple loop that respects their context. Right now Next() is semi-blocking and Close() can be racy with internal reconnects.

maya: Proposed small API tweaks: 1) Add NextCtx(ctx) which returns (bool) and makes cancel behavior deterministic. 2) Make Close() idempotent and never panic. 3) Return typed errors: ErrCanceled for user ctx cancel, ErrRetryable for transient transport/auth hiccups, ErrClosed for double-close.

ben: I like NextCtx. Example snippet for quickstart:```go
ctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), 10*time.Second)
defer cancel()
g := client.Generator(ctx, model, nil)
defer g.Close()
for g.NextCtx(ctx) {
  fmt.Print(g.Value().Text)
}
if err := g.Err(); err != nil {
  if errors.Is(err, sdk.ErrCanceled) {
    // normal cancellation
  } else if errors.Is(err, sdk.ErrRetryable) {
    // transient, maybe retry
  } else {
    log.Fatal(err)
  }
}
```

maya: That snippet would address most onboarding questions. Also add a short explanation in quickstart about long-lived streams: prefer resumable logic on ErrRetryable vs abort on ErrCanceled.

owen: For implementation: use an internal select in NextCtx on user ctx and internal message channel; Close should use sync.Once to guarantee idempotence. Tests: simulate auth token refresh by forcing auth middleware to return 401 twice then succeed and run the loop with context deadlines to ensure no leaks.

ben: Docs note: call out how generator state maps to errors so app authors know whether to resume or re-create the generator. Also, add a one-file sample in go-sdk-samples titled "generator-cancel-and-retry" linked from quickstart.

maya: I'll file a PR with the three changes + sample + docs blurb and ping eng and docs for review.

docs-bot: reminder: update changelog and migration guide if API changes land.
